Notebook[{Cell["Quantum majority vote", "Title"],
  Cell[
   "Three inputs, one output; exact optimization for d \[GreaterEqual] 3",
   "Subtitle"], Cell["This notebook implements the majority-vote LP of \
Section 7.2, equations (155)\[Dash](158). It loads Sage-generated primitive \
idempotents of the walled Brauer algebra and maximizes the worst-case success \
probability over the three input classes. The expected optimum is 8/9.",
   "Text"], Cell["Evaluate the notebook from top to bottom. The default \
dimension is d = 4; any integer d \[GreaterEqual] 3 is supported. \
Diagram-coefficient matching for trace preservation requires d \
\[GreaterEqual] p = 3, so this implementation does not cover d = 2. The d = 3 \
database has nine paths; the generic database has ten.", "Text"],
  Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["1. Parameters and local data", "Section"],
